// Re-derive the Chrome VA-API desktop-entry override after every dpkg run.
//
// Why: /usr/local/share/applications/google-chrome.desktop is a whole-file
// copy of the packaged /usr/share/applications/google-chrome.desktop with one
// launch flag added, and /usr/local/share precedes /usr/share in
// XDG_DATA_DIRS, so the copy wins for every user. A Chrome upgrade rewrites
// the packaged file; the copy keeps winning regardless, so a key the new
// release added is simply absent from the entry the desktop actually uses.
// Nothing about that failure points at VA-API, which is the only reason this
// copy exists.
//
// Why a hook and not just the provisioning script: the copy goes out of date
// when Chrome upgrades, not when the machine is provisioned, and nothing ties
// those two moments together.
//
// Scope: the script writes nothing when the result is unchanged, and removes
// the override outright if Chrome is uninstalled. It fails the transaction if
// Chrome's Exec= shape stops matching the pattern it rewrites -- a silently
// flagless launcher is indistinguishable from success until a video fails to
// play, so that case has to be loud.
//
// Revert: rm this file, /usr/local/sbin/regenerate-chrome-vaapi-override and
// /usr/local/share/applications/google-chrome.desktop, then
// update-desktop-database /usr/local/share/applications
DPkg::Post-Invoke {
    "if [ -x /usr/local/sbin/regenerate-chrome-vaapi-override ]; then /usr/local/sbin/regenerate-chrome-vaapi-override; fi";
};
